Looking for Richard is a 1996 American documentary film
directed by Al Pacino, in his directorial debut.

11
01:22:08,000 --> 01:22:14,000
It is a hybrid film, including both a filmed performance of selected scenes of William Shakespeare's Richard III and a documentary
element which explores a broader examination of Shakespeare's continuing role and relevance in popular culture.

12
01:29:36,000 --> 01:29:42,000
The film was featured at the Sundance Film Festival in January 1996 and it was
screened in the Un Certain Regard section at the 1996 Cannes Film Festival.

13
01:37:04,000 --> 01:37:10,000
Al Pacino won the Directors Guild of America Award for
Outstanding Directing – Documentaries.

